        "synopsis": {
            "value": "Set during the year 1999, when some people thought the end of the world was approaching, Eun Chae-Ni (Park Eun-Bin) lives in Haeseong City. Her only relative is her grandmother Kim Jeon-Bok (Kim Hae-Sook), who runs a well known restaurant in Haeseong. Eun Chae-Ni is an unpredictable person with a bright personality. One day, she is caught up in an unexpected incident and suddenly gains a supernatural power. When this occurs, she happens to be with her neighbors Son Gyeong-Hun (Choi Dae-Hoon) and Kang Ro-Bin (Im Sung-Jae). They also gain their own supernatural powers, but their supernatural powers are not perfect.\n\nMeanwhile, Lee Un-Jeong (Cha Eun-Woo) arrived in Haeseong City from Seoul and has been working as a civil servant at the local city hall. He is very strict with keeping his principles and he lacks social skills at his work. Outside of city hall, he is a bit of a mysterious person. He approaches the series of disappearances that takes place in Haeseong City with Eun Chae-Ni. Ha Won-Do (Son Hyun-Joo) seems like a cool-headed and rational person, but he has a dark desire behind that veneer. Eun Chae-Ni and her neighbors Son Gyeong-Hun and Kang Ro-Bin, who have gained supernatural powers unexpectedly, fight against a villain who threatens the peace of Haeseong City.",
            "source": "asianwiki",
            "source_link": "https://asianwiki.com/The_WONDERfools"
